  "equipment_type": "VAV / zone damper controller (Verasys)",
  "applies_to": "Verasys Zone Equipment Controllers serving zone dampers and VAV boxes in a Verasys zoning system.",
  "summary": "The Zone Equipment Controller runs one zone of a Verasys zoning system (zone damper or VAV box, optional reheat). Through the SBH it exposes 57 objects in the 90,000 range: zone and discharge temperatures, occupied/unoccupied/standby setpoints, airflow limits, damper limits, DCV settings, enables, occupancy mode and zone vote.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Object names are the short Verasys names as printed. The guide gives no units or state texts; multistate state texts come from the device.",
    "Access is from the Writable column (TRUE = writable).",
    "Printed instances are base values (the Attribute column). Each zone controller adds MAC address x 100: a ZEC at MAC 5 serves ZN-T as AV 90,500 (90,000 + 5 x 100).",
    "Source: LIT-12013287 Table 3 'BACnet attributes' (57 objects)."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Verasys BACnet over IP Integration User Guide",
    "doc_number": "LIT-12013287",
    "revision_date": "2024-03-11",
    "url": "https://docs.johnsoncontrols.com/bas/api/khub/maps/bQUUXbLn_sJI5F5XzKax0Q/attachments/ETDjFYqCzPvla4mPr0wdlw-bQUUXbLn_sJI5F5XzKax0Q/content"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Integrate through the Verasys Smart Building Hub: enable BACnet routing on the SBH, and the supervisor then sees each system bus device behind the SBH's MS/TP network. Map the enable and occupancy commands, the main setpoints and the status and alarm points.",
